{"timestamp": 1779403009.166919, "event_type": "phase_changed", "tick": 26, "data": {"phase": "discussion"}}
{"timestamp": 1779403026.56847, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 26, "data": {"player_id": "player_2", "message": "I found Alice's body down in the lower engine. Listen up, because there are only three of us left (me, Bob, and Eve), which means we have to get this right or the Duck wins. \n\nHere is my exact path: security, electrical, medbay, storage, and finally lower engine where I found the body. \n\nBob, I saw you a couple of times. I saw you in medbay around tick 16, and then again in storage around tick 21. You left storage heading back towards medbay right before I walked down into lower engine and found Alice. \n\nEve, I haven't seen you this entire round. Where have you been, and what tasks were you doing? \n\nBob, please confirm our encounters. Between you two, I'm leaning slightly towards Eve because she's been completely off the radar while I can somewhat track Bob's movements, but I need to hear both of your full paths before we vote. Let's talk this out."}}
{"timestamp": 1779403045.3408089, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 26, "data": {"player_id": "player_1", "message": "Charlie's story is completely accurate, which honestly makes me trust him a lot more. \n\nMy exact path was cafeteria -> medbay -> storage -> medbay -> cafeteria. I did see Charlie in medbay around tick 17, and then he came into storage from medbay right around tick 21 while I was in there. I left storage heading back up north, and he went south towards lower engine where he found the body. \n\nIf Charlie were the Duck, he could have easily lied right here to frame me for a Lylo win by saying I ran out of lower engine. Instead, he told the exact truth about my movements. Because of that, and because I also haven't seen Eve *at all* this entire round, Eve is my prime suspect right now. \n\nEve, you are the last to speak. We are at final three, so this is for the game. Where were you, what tasks were you doing, and why didn't either of us see you? Your path better be incredibly detailed. I'm leaning heavily towards voting Eve, but I will listen to what she has to say."}}
{"timestamp": 1779403086.439106, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 26, "data": {"player_id": "player_4", "message": "Okay, listen carefully because I have actual information that changes this whole picture.\n\nMy full route: storage -> lower engine -> upper engine -> oxygen -> cafeteria -> medbay -> electrical, which is where I am right now. I was doing engine calibration tasks and oxygen filter tasks, which is why I was on the outer loop of the ship the whole time and you two \u2014 who were stuck in the middle corridor between medbay and storage \u2014 never crossed me.\n\nNow here's the critical part. I was in lower engine early in the round, around tick 15, and **Alice was alive in lower engine when I was there.** I saw her with my own eyes. I did my engine task and moved up to upper engine, then oxygen. Alice was still alive when I left.\n\nSo think about who went into lower engine AFTER me. Bob, by your own admission, you never went south of storage \u2014 your loop was cafeteria/medbay/storage. Fine. But Charlie? Charlie says he walked into lower engine and \"found\" Alice's body. Charlie, you were the LAST person in that room with her, and you're the one who reported. That's the textbook Duck play \u2014 kill in an isolated room, report the body yourself to control the narrative, and pin it on the player nobody saw.\n\nAnd Charlie, notice what you did in your speech \u2014 you vouched for Bob's movements very precisely to lock in a 2v1 against me. Of course you told the truth about Bob, because Bob is your shield. You needed Bob to trust you so you could swing his vote onto me.\n\nBob, I'm asking you to think. I saw Alice alive in lower engine. Charlie found her dead in lower engine. The simplest explanation is Charlie killed her between those two moments. If you vote me out and I'm a Goose, the Duck wins instantly. Vote Charlie. I'm voting Charlie."}}
